From: Liuqin Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: sensor: add IMX596 cell size and control delays

The stock AAC module declares 0.8 um cells and two-frame delays for both
line count and gain. Preserve the generic blanking delays: simple only
uses the exposure/gain delays and blanking response remains unmeasured.

diff --git a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
index 28043150..e0089703 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -309,6 +309,18 @@ const CameraSensorProperties *CameraSensorProperties::get(const std::string &sen
 				.hblankDelay = 3
 			},
 		} },
+		{ "imx596", {
+			/* AAC module: 0.8 um cells, two-frame exposure/gain delay. */
+			.unitCellSize = { 800, 800 },
+			.testPatternModes = {},
+			.sensorDelays = {
+				.exposureDelay = 2,
+				.gainDelay = 2,
+				/* Keep the legacy defaults for unused blanking delays. */
+				.vblankDelay = 2,
+				.hblankDelay = 2
+			},
+		} },
 		{ "imx678", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 2000, 2000 },
 			.testPatternModes = {},
